# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own Prisma Postgres connection
# strings (see README's "PostgreSQL構成" section for how to get these from
# https://console.prisma.io — create a free/Starter database, region
# ap-northeast-1). Never commit real values here.
#
# Prisma Console currently offers exactly two connection string formats per
# database ("Prisma ORM" and "Any client" tabs) — there is no separate
# pooled-TCP option, so this project uses both formats below rather than
# inventing one.

# Prisma Accelerate connection string ("Prisma ORM" tab) — used by the app
# at runtime (src/lib/prisma.ts) via `accelerateUrl` +
# @prisma/extension-accelerate, which pools connections so a serverless
# environment like Vercel doesn't exhaust the database.
DATABASE_URL="prisma+postgres://accelerate.prisma-data.net/?api_key=..."

# Direct (plain TCP) connection ("Any client" tab) — used by the Prisma CLI
# for migrations (see prisma.config.ts) and by prisma/seed.ts via the
# @prisma/adapter-pg driver adapter, so those don't go through Accelerate.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@db.prisma.io:5432/?sslmode=require"
